          "source_quote": "οἶδα γὰρ ὅτι ἔνεστιν ὧν βούλεταί τις καὶ ταχέως λαβεῖν καὶ βραδέως μὴ τυχεῖν",
          "english_quote": "For I know that there are things a person wants both to receive quickly and not to obtain slowly.",
          "issue": "The natural impersonal analysis takes ἔνεστιν as “it is possible,” governing the coordinated infinitives λαβεῖν and μὴ τυχεῖν, while ὧν βούλεταί τις identifies what someone desires. The draft instead substitutes an existential assertion and makes both outcomes objects of desire. Its note neither establishes that existential analysis nor discloses the materially different modal reading. This concerns syntax and lexical meaning in the verified print, not evidence of source corruption.",
          "suggested_revision": "Reassess the infinitives’ attachment and preserve the potentiality expressed by ἔνεστιν. A candidate requiring fresh review is: “For I know that it is possible both to receive quickly what one wants and not to obtain it after a long delay.” Explain the contrast between quick receipt and prolonged nonattainment in the note. If retaining the existential/preference analysis, supply a defensible grammatical justification and disclose the modal alternative; do not treat the current rationale as sufficient.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ βραδέως μὴ τυχεῖν",
          "english_quote": "This closely preserves the unusual coordination. The second member reinforces the wish for prompt receipt; taking it instead as “not to miss obtaining even slowly” is possible only by assigning the negation and adverb a less immediate scope.",
          "issue": "The proposed alternative “not to miss obtaining” is not supported by the printed τυχεῖν, which here means to obtain or attain, not to miss obtaining. With μὴ, the phrase expresses nonattainment. Changing the adverb’s scope does not supply the additional negative idea needed to turn it into successful attainment. Consequently, the note does not faithfully preserve a viable alternative.",
          "suggested_revision": "Remove “not to miss obtaining even slowly.” Replace the rationale with an explanation of genuine attachment and scope alternatives, especially whether the infinitives express possibilities under ἔνεστιν or wishes under βούλεται. Preserve nonattainment wherever μὴ τυχεῖν is translated; do not introduce an unprinted verb or negate an invented failure term.",
